<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="56388" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/EPSY/590/56388.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2025" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025.xml">2025</calendarYear><term id="120251" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring.xml">Spring 2025</term><subject id="EPSY" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/EPSY.xml">Educational Psychology</subject><course id="590" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/EPSY/590.xml">Advanced Seminar in Educational Psychology</course></parents><sectionNumber>BBB</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Biological Basis of Behavior</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Course explores human brain structure and function as they pertain to behavior. It covers topics such as functional neuroanatomy including organization of the nervous system, electrical and chemical conduction, hormones, sensation, pain, sexual activity, memory, addiction, emotion, mental disorders and treatment modalities for mental disorders in view of brain structure and function.  Day1Access course materials cost $54.89. For more information see https://go.illinois.edu/Day1Access.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Open (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2025-01-21Z</startDate><endDate>2025-05-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="ONL">Online</type><start>ARRANGED</start><instructors><instructor lastName="Sauer" firstName="J">Sauer, J</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>